{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the entire application draft, including all claims, the detailed description, all other prose sections, the reference numeral ledger, and all figure briefs. Every limitation in every one of the 20 claims, every numbered part, and every technical assertion in the description and other sections was traced to an affirmative statement in the inventor's disclosure or conversation history. The review also confirmed internal consistency across all parts of the application. One unsupported geometric detail was found in a figure brief.\n\nThe figure brief for FIG. 2 specifies that the legs of the perimeter member are \"flush with\" the ends of the base. This is a specific relative positioning that is not described or supported by the inventor's source materials, which only state that the perimeter member is \"at a perimeter\" of the base's second side. This unsupported detail will be removed to ensure all specifications are strictly faithful to the source disclosure. No other issues were found. The remainder of the application is fully supported and internally consistent."}
